 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Completed the Ready precondition on {{v1}} (\"{{v2}}\"). The blocked precondition was supplier-related: Part B (\"{{v4}}\") had no supplier, and the app requires every part to have a supplier before the ticket can go Ready. I edited that part via its row \"Edit\" button (opened the \"Edit part\" dialog with Part name*, Cost*, Markup %*, Quantity, Supplier), set Supplier = \"{{v5}}\" and left Cost = $200.00 and Markup % = 25, then clicked \"Save part\". The parts table then showed both parts with a supplier: {{v3}} RD Part A | $150.00 | 25% | qty 1 | {{v5}} | $187.50 and {{v4}} | $200.00 | 25% | qty 1 | {{v5}} | $250.00, total (price × quantity) $437.50. I then clicked the \"Mark Ready\" button in the ticket header; the status badge changed from Draft to Ready (the header button row re-rendered to \"Mark Draft\" / \"Mark Closed\"), with no error or confirmation toast — the status badge update is the confirmation. Note: a replayed stored procedure had already performed the supplier edit (steps 1–3) before failing at its status click, so I did not repeat that edit and only performed the \"Mark Ready\" click.",
